{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S8RDUNmQzvgWMZJ9tuXWK9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"start\" \"end\" units %lthr API\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"},{\"title\":\"9822 convert training prescriptions to intervalsicu workouts with claude opus ai\",\"url\":\"https://n8n.io/workflows/9822-convert-training-prescriptions-to-intervalsicu-workouts-with-claude-opus-ai/\"},{\"title\":\"Workout builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839\"}]\n\nThe search turned up no official documentation for the `workout_doc` HR target fields. The useful material comes from Intervals.icu forum threads and a third-party tool, so treat it as community-sourced.\n\n- **Power example and range fields:** A forum post shows a `workout_doc` where a power step carries a `power` object plus a `_power` object with `start` and `end` values, and the poster says the FTP sits alongside it so the `_power` range can be converted into a percentage. For power the athlete's FTP is included in the workout_doc field. The same thread says the `_power` range is generated automatically: Intervals.icu translates fixed power (and other) targets into a range.\n- **HR range width:** The default range for power and pace is 2.5%. For HR it is 1.5%. The range can be overridden with an `hrRange` query parameter, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **LTHR fields:** A developer said they have added these fields to workout_doc, including an integer `lthr` and a `threshold_pace`, which is the basis for expressing HR targets relative to LTHR.\n- **Sending HR as % LTHR:** A Garmin-related thread says the target HR is sent as % of LTHR, and that sending as % LTHR is done so that workouts can be exchanged with other users.\n- **Units format:** A forum post shows power steps using \"units\": \"%ftp\". I did not find a confirmed example of an HR step using `%lthr` as its units value, so check that against the inspector or a downloaded workout.\n- **Missing official docs:** One developer said not yet when asked about full REST API documentation, and suggested that many mirror the private API endpoints used by the Intervals.icu web app. So you can use the inspector to see what to send and what comes back. Replace /api/ with /api/v1/ in the path.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddabbd87-b75f-4e07-9388-c2604810bbe5","uuid":"a8d0a773-c082-4135-8d3d-e13b7cac5eaf","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:05:01.862Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"start\" \"end\" units %lthr API","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014iFhKabMdCKViBRU3nn2pZ","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389"},{"title":"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md"},{"title":"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157"},{"title":"9822 convert training prescriptions to intervalsicu workouts with claude opus ai","url":"https://n8n.io/workflows/9822-convert-training-prescriptions-to-intervalsicu-workouts-with-claude-opus-ai/"},{"title":"Workout builder","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839"}]},"The search turned up no official documentation for the `workout_doc` HR target fields. The useful material comes from Intervals.icu forum threads and a third-party tool, so treat it as community-sourced.\n\n- **Power example and range fields:** A forum post shows a `workout_doc` where a power step carries a `power` object plus a `_power` object with `start` and `end` values, and the poster says the FTP sits alongside it so the `_power` range can be converted into a percentage. For power the athlete's FTP is included in the workout_doc field. The same thread says the `_power` range is generated automatically: Intervals.icu translates fixed power (and other) targets into a range.\n- **HR range width:** The default range for power and pace is 2.5%. For HR it is 1.5%. The range can be overridden with an `hrRange` query parameter, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **LTHR fields:** A developer said they have added these fields to workout_doc, including an integer `lthr` and a `threshold_pace`, which is the basis for expressing HR targets relative to LTHR.\n- **Sending HR as % LTHR:** A Garmin-related thread says the target HR is sent as % of LTHR, and that sending as % LTHR is done so that workouts can be exchanged with other users.\n- **Units format:** A forum post shows power steps using \"units\": \"%ftp\". I did not find a confirmed example of an HR step using `%lthr` as its units value, so check that against the inspector or a downloaded workout.\n- **Missing official docs:** One developer said not yet when asked about full REST API documentation, and suggested that many mirror the private API endpoints used by the Intervals.icu web app. So you can use the inspector to see what to send and what comes back. Replace /api/ with /api/v1/ in the path."],"durationSeconds":7.570402708,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S8RDUNmQzvgWMZJ9tuXWK9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
